 "storyArc": "Hernando tells them how the café was when he first came in 1979: there was a jukebox, Rosa was thirty and had a temper, and the whole street smelled of her pandeyucas. Repairing the counter, Tomás pulls out a loose brick and finds Rosa's recipe notebook, and inside it an unsent letter, forty-seven years old, addressed to \"Joaquín\". Vale reads the first line and goes pale.",
